Here is the SQL query to drop all available tables:

SET FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS = 0;
DROP TABLE IF TABLE EXISTS `table1`, `table2`, ...;  # replace with your table names
SET FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS = 1;

If you don't know the table names, you can use the following query to dynamically generate the DROP TABLE statements:

SET FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS = 0;
SET @tables = NULL;
SELECT GROUP_CONCAT(TABLE_SCHEMA, '.', TABLE_NAME) INTO @tables
  FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES
  WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'your_database_name';  # replace with your database name
SELECT IF (@tables IS NULL, 'FAILURE', CONCAT('DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ', @tables, '; SUCCESS')) INTO @query;
PREPARE stmt FROM @query;
EXECUTE stmt;
DEALLOCATE PREPARE stmt;
SET FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS = 1;

Replace 'your_database_name' with the name of your database.
